cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BILBO in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "BILBO: Bilayer Lipid Builder and Organizer for protein and peptide membrane systems"
abstract: >-
  BILBO is an end-to-end pipeline that builds flat lipid bilayer membranes
  from all-atom PDB templates, places proteins or peptides on or inside the
  bilayer, optionally solvates the system with explicit water and counter
  ions, and exports a self-contained GROMACS molecular dynamics package.
  The exported package bundles the CHARMM36 force field, MDP files, and a
  run script, producing a ready-to-minimize starting structure. BILBO ships
  as a Python CLI and an optional web interface, with deterministic outputs
  and a complete provenance manifest of input, parameters, and generated
  files.
